The lock screen's fonts, loaded into GNOME Shell's process only (never
installed into the system): shell/core/fonts.js adds them to the shell's
font maps, lib/glyphOutlines.js reads their outlines for the glass clock.

Inter.ttf
    Inter 4.001, variable: wght 100–900, opsz 14–32.
    From https://github.com/google/fonts/blob/main/ofl/inter/Inter%5Bopsz,wght%5D.ttf
    (there named Inter[opsz,wght].ttf).
    sha256 29160a80ff49ddcab2c97711247e08b1fab27a484a329ce8b813d820dc559031
    Copyright 2020 The Inter Project Authors (https://github.com/rsms/inter),
    SIL Open Font License 1.1: Inter-OFL.txt.

RobotoFlex.ttf
    Roboto Flex 3.200, variable: wght 100–1000, wdth 25–151, opsz 8–144,
    GRAD, XOPQ, XTRA, YOPQ, YTAS, YTDE, YTFI, YTLC, YTUC, slnt.
    From https://github.com/google/fonts/blob/main/ofl/robotoflex/RobotoFlex%5BGRAD,XOPQ,XTRA,YOPQ,YTAS,YTDE,YTFI,YTLC,YTUC,opsz,slnt,wdth,wght%5D.ttf
    (there named RobotoFlex[GRAD,XOPQ,XTRA,YOPQ,YTAS,YTDE,YTFI,YTLC,YTUC,opsz,slnt,wdth,wght].ttf).
    sha256 9b523f7d82593df0107173849ebb8c817471a1df4b4fb2c3cbf40cfd810c8281
    Copyright 2017 The Roboto Flex Project Authors
    (https://github.com/TypeNetwork/Roboto-Flex),
    SIL Open Font License 1.1: RobotoFlex-OFL.txt.

The files are as published, only renamed (the fonts' own names are kept).
